<title>USA: U.S. exporters sell 250,000 tonnes wheat to Egypt.</title>
<headline>U.S. exporters sell 250,000 tonnes wheat to Egypt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. exporters reported sales of 250,000 tonnes of soft red winter wheat to Egypt for delivery during the 1997/98 marketing year, the Agriculture Department said Thursday.</p>
<p>The marketing year for wheat begins June 1.</p>
<p>Exporters are required to report to USDA any export sales of 100,000 tonnes or more of one commodity to one destination by 1500 EDT on the next business day following the sale.</p>
<p>((--Washington commodities desk 202 898 8467))</p>
